const UI = `ROLE: ui (UI kit + app shell). Your port: 5181.
Build the shared UI kit in src/ui/ that every feature screen will use, so the whole app looks like ONE coherent product matching docs/reference (BRIEF section 2). Feature agents start as soon as you finish: finish the kit completely and document it.
Keep the existing exports of src/ui/index.tsx working (Icon, IconComponent, AppFrame, Page, TabBar, ToastProvider, useToast) - rewrite their implementation freely. Split into files (e.g. src/ui/Button.tsx + Button.css) and re-export everything from src/ui/index.tsx.
Components (Spanish aria-labels; ALL colors from tokens; motion from 'motion/react'):
- Icon({icon, size=24, className}) - keep; adds class ui-icon.
- AppFrame - centered column (max --app-max), min-height 100dvh, page background visible around it on desktop.
- Page({children, tabBar?: boolean=false (bottom padding for the floating tab bar), variant?: 'tab'|'push'='push' (tab = fade + 12px vertical; push = horizontal slide), padded?: boolean=true, className?}) - motion root for page transitions (App uses AnimatePresence mode="wait" keyed by pathname), safe-area top padding, --gutter side padding.
- TopBar({title?, subtitle?, left?, right?, large?: boolean (big bold title like "Explore" in ref-1), sticky?: boolean}).
- BackButton({fallback='/'}) - ChevronLeft icon button: navigate(-1) when there is history, else fallback.
- IconButton({icon, label (aria-label, required), onClick, variant: 'ghost'|'surface'|'neu'|'ink'|'accent'='ghost', size: 'sm'(36)|'md'(44)|'lg'(56)|'xl'(76)='md', active?, disabled?, type?, className?}) - round, whileTap scale.
- Button({children, variant: 'ink'|'accent'|'secondary'|'ghost'|'danger'='ink', size: 'sm'|'md'|'lg'='md', icon?, iconRight?, full?, loading?, disabled?, onClick, type?}) - pill; 'ink' = the black pill with white text from ref-1 "Play"; 'secondary' = surface-2 pill.
- Card({children, padding?: 'none'|'sm'|'md'|'lg'='md', interactive?, onClick?, glass?, className?, style?}).
- Sheet({open, onClose, title?, children, footer?, height?: 'auto'|'tall'}) - bottom sheet in a portal: scrim fade, spring slide-up, drag handle, drag-down-to-dismiss (motion drag="y"), Escape closes, focus moved into the sheet, body scroll lock, scrollable content, safe-area bottom padding, top corners --r-xl.
- ActionSheet({open, onClose, title?, actions: {key?, label, icon?, onSelect, tone?: 'danger', disabled?}[]}) - built on Sheet; selecting closes then runs the action.
- ConfirmDialog({open, title, message?, confirmLabel='Aceptar', cancelLabel='Cancelar', tone?: 'danger', onConfirm, onCancel}).
- PromptDialog({open, title, initialValue, placeholder?, confirmLabel='Guardar', onConfirm(value), onCancel, maxLength?}) - autofocus + select, Enter submits.
- Segmented<T extends string|number>({options: {value, label?, icon?, ariaLabel?}[], value, onChange, size?: 'sm'|'md', full?}) - sliding pill indicator via motion layoutId (unique per instance via useId).
- Slider({value, min, max, step=1, onChange, onChangeEnd?, ariaLabel, format?, showValue?}) - native input range for a11y, custom track/fill/thumb, large touch area.
- RangeSlider({value: [a,b], min, max, step=1, onChange, onChangeEnd?, ariaLabel, format?}) - two thumbs.
- Toggle({checked, onChange, ariaLabel?, disabled?}) - switch with spring knob.
- Stepper({value, min, max, step=1, onChange, format?, ariaLabel}) - minus/value/plus with Minus/Plus icons, press-and-hold repeat.
- Chip({selected?, onClick, children, icon?}) and ChipRow({children}) - horizontal scroll, hidden scrollbar, edge fade.
- SearchField({value, onChange, placeholder='Buscar', onClear?, autoFocus?}) - light pill like ref-3 with SearchMd icon and XClose clear.
- ListRow({leading?, title, subtitle?, trailing?, onClick?, chevron?, tone?: 'danger', disabled?}).
- SettingsGroup({title?, children, footer?}) - card with rows separated by hairlines.
- SectionHeader({title, action?: {label, onClick}}).
- EmptyState({image?, title, action?}) - calm, centered, lots of space.
- Cover({src?, seed, size, shape: 'circle'|'rounded'='rounded', spinning?, alt?, className?}) - image cover; when no src, a generated soft tonal placeholder from the seed (token colors + subtle staff-lines motif, no text).
- Vinyl({size=260, spinning, speed?: 'slow'|'normal', label?: ReactNode, labelSrc?: string, tonearm?: 'rest'|'play'|'hidden'='hidden', progress?: number (0..1 thin accent ring), onClick?, ariaLabel?}) - THE signature component (ref-1 turntable): black vinyl with subtle grooves (repeating-radial-gradient) and a soft specular highlight, center label (image or content), optional soft neumorphic round plinth, an SVG tonearm that rotates onto the record when 'play'. Spinning: continuous linear rotation that eases in/out when toggled (no jumps). Reduced motion: no spin.
- Waveform({peaks: ArrayLike<number> (0..1), progress?, selection?: [number, number] (0..1, dims outside), height=72, barWidth=3, gap=2, className?}) - crisp rounded bars at devicePixelRatio, responsive width.
- LiveBars({level (0..1), bars=24, height=48, active?}) - live level bars like ref-1's waveform glyph (center bars taller, smooth attack/decay).
- ProgressRing({value (0..1), size=280, stroke=4, children?, indeterminate?}).
- Spinner({size=20}).
- Toasts via ToastProvider/useToast().show(message, {tone?: 'neutral'|'success'|'danger'}) - small pill at the top (safe area), motion enter/exit, auto-dismiss ~2.6 s.
- TabBar({visible}) - floating glass pill centered at the bottom above the safe area; 3 icon-only items: Inicio ('/', Home02), Biblioteca ('/library', BookOpen01 or similar), Ajustes ('/settings', Settings01); active = ink with a soft indicator (layoutId), inactive = ink-3; slides away when not visible. aria-labels.
- src/ui/motion.ts - shared presets: ease, spring, pageVariants, fadeUp(delay), listContainer/listItem (stagger ~0.04).
- Hooks: useLongPress(cb, ms), useReducedMotionPref() (OS preference + settings.reduceMotion from src/state/settings).
Styling: co-located CSS files with the 'ui-' prefix. tokens.css is lead-owned: if you need extra tokens define them in src/ui/kit.css under :root (and its dark-mode equivalents) and mention them. You own src/styles/global.css. In App.tsx you may adjust ONLY shell/transition wiring (keep every route and import) and add a DEV-only gallery route '/__kit' (guarded by import.meta.env.DEV) rendering every component from src/ui/KitGallery.tsx. Screenshot the gallery full-page in light and dark (docs/screenshots/ui-kit-light.png / ui-kit-dark.png) and iterate until it looks refined and coherent with the references (soft, airy, consistent radii and shadows, no visual noise).
Write docs/UI-KIT.md: concise API reference for every export with a one-line usage example each, plus layout recipes (screen skeleton: TopBar + content + bottom actions; sticky bottom bar above the safe area; spacing scale). Feature agents rely on it.
Verification: typecheck clean for src/ui and App.tsx; npm run build succeeds.`

const AUDIO = `ROLE: engine-audio (audio I/O + transcription). Your port: 5182.
Implement src/engine/audio/ and src/engine/transcribe/ behind the declared signatures (both index.ts files are the contract). Add exports freely, never break existing ones.
1. Model: copy node_modules/@spotify/basic-pitch/model/{model.json,group1-shard1of1.bin} into public/models/basic-pitch/ plus its Apache-2.0 LICENSE. Compute the model URL on the MAIN thread as new URL('models/basic-pitch/model.json', document.baseURI).href and pass it to the worker (base is './', worker-relative URLs would break).
2. Worker src/engine/transcribe/worker.ts (new Worker(new URL('./worker.ts', import.meta.url), { type: 'module' })): imports @tensorflow/tfjs 3.21 + @spotify/basic-pitch. Read node_modules/@spotify/basic-pitch/types and its src to use the exact API (BasicPitch class, evaluateModel(audio, onComplete(frames, onsets, contours), percentCallback), outputToNotesPoly(frames, onsets, onsetThresh, frameThresh, minNoteLen, inferOnsets, maxFreq, minFreq, melodiaTrick, energyTolerance), addPitchBendsToNoteEvents, noteFramesToTime). Backend: try 'webgl' (OffscreenCanvas in the worker), fall back to 'cpu'; log the backend once. ONE long-lived worker keeps the model loaded; cancel() terminates it (recreated lazily); preloadModel() warms it up. Piano range only (A0-C8). Map sensitivity (0..1) and minNoteMs to thresholds; calibrate with the fixtures below so sensitivity 0.5 gives the best F1. Output NoteEvent[] sorted by start (velocity = amplitude clamped 0..1). Progress stages: 'loading-model' (0-0.1), 'analyzing' (0.1-0.9 from percentCallback), 'extracting-notes' (0.9-1). tfjs/basic-pitch must ONLY be imported inside the worker (lean main bundle). Errors reject with short Spanish messages.
3. Audio: decodeMediaFile (audio AND video containers via decodeAudioData; close contexts; kind from MIME/extension; Spanish error "No se pudo leer el audio de este archivo. Prueba con MP3, WAV, M4A o MP4."), toModelInput (OfflineAudioContext(1, n, 22050) render = mono + resample + crop, then peak-normalize to 0.95), computePeaks, startRecording (mic: getUserMedia with echoCancellation/noiseSuppression/autoGainControl false; tab: getDisplayMedia({video: true, audio: true, systemAudio: 'include'}) -> Spanish error if no audio track was shared, stop video tracks; MediaRecorder with the best supported mime; AnalyserNode RMS -> perceptual 0..1 level at ~30 Hz via onLevel; maxSeconds auto-stop; stop()/cancel() release all tracks and contexts), isMicSupported, isTabCaptureSupported (getDisplayMedia present and not a touch-primary/mobile device). ALSO export encodeWav(samples: Float32Array, sampleRate: number): Blob (16-bit PCM mono) - the capture flow stores trimmed file audio with it.
4. Fixtures + accuracy (the fixtures already exist in test/fixtures/; sox is not installed on Windows, so do not regenerate them): scripts/fixtures/make-fixtures.sh (sox/ffmpeg) generating into test/fixtures/: scale.wav (C major scale C4-C5 quarter notes at 100 BPM, piano-like timbre e.g. sox synth pluck with a decay envelope), chords.wav (C-F-G-C block triads in half notes at 90 BPM with bass notes), melody-bass.wav (melody in eighths over a bass line in quarters at 110 BPM, G major, ~8 s), scale.mp4 (video track + the scale audio; pick an encoder that exists here: check ffmpeg -encoders), and ground-truth JSON per WAV ({pitch, start, duration}[] + bpm). Browser harness: test/harness/transcribe.html + test/harness/transcribe.ts (served by the Vite dev server) that fetches a fixture, decodes it with decodeMediaFile, toModelInput, transcribe, and exposes results on window.__result; scripts/fixtures/check-transcription.mjs (puppeteer-core) runs every fixture and prints precision/recall/F1 (exact pitch, onset within 60 ms), runtime and backend. Iterate on thresholds/defaults until scale F1 >= 0.9 and chords/melody-bass are as good as you can get; report the numbers. Verify the mp4 decodes.
5. Unit tests (vitest, node env) for pure helpers (threshold mapping, WAV header, peaks).
Verification: typecheck clean for your files, npm test, npm run build (worker emitted as its own chunk; main chunk must not contain tfjs).`

const SCORE = `ROLE: engine-score (music analysis + notation). Optional port for visual checks: 5183.
Implement src/engine/score/ behind src/engine/score/index.ts (read it and src/types.ts: they are the contract). Pure TypeScript, no DOM, deterministic. Split into files (analysis, keys, spelling, quantize, build, abc, musicxml, midi...) and re-export from index.ts. Also implement src/data/demos.ts.
A. analyzeNotes: tempo from an onset-strength envelope (note onsets weighted by velocity, chord notes merged within ~30 ms) at 100 Hz; autocorrelation/comb filter over 50-200 BPM with a mild log-normal prior around 110 BPM; resolve half/double errors by which grid explains the onsets best; integer bpm; bpmConfidence 0..1. Beat phase: beatOffset maximizing weighted onset alignment; choose the downbeat with bass-note/velocity accents; document how you handle offsets before the first note. Meter: 4/4 default; 3/4 only when 3-beat accent periodicity clearly wins (6/8 only by user choice). Key: Krumhansl-Kessler or Temperley profiles on a duration x velocity pitch-class histogram, best of 24; keyConfidence from the margin; conventional spelling (fewest accidentals). Empty input: 100 bpm, offset 0, 4/4, C major, confidences 0. Never throw.
B. defaultParams: bpm/beatOffset/timeSignature from analysis, key null (auto), quantize/splitPoint/difficulty from settings, transpose 0, minVelocity 0.1, minDuration 0.05, pitchRange [21,108], maxPolyphony 4 (choose sensibly).
C. buildScore (< 30 ms for 3 000 notes, never throw): 1) filter by velocity/duration/range, transpose (clamp 21..108), key = (params.key ?? analysis.key) transposed. 2) seconds -> ticks (1 tick = 16th): (t - beatOffset)/(60/bpm)*4; snap onsets to the grid (16 -> 1 tick, 8 -> 2 ticks), snap ends, min one grid unit; shift by whole measures so the first note lands in measure 0; startSeconds = time of tick 0. 3) merge duplicates (same pitch+onset keep longest), cut same-pitch overlaps. 4) hands: pitch >= splitPoint right, else left (light heuristic allowed: keep a chord straddling the split by <= 2 semitones in its majority hand). 5) difficulty: original as is; intermedio = 8th grid, polyphony <= 3, drop the quietest notes of dense clusters; facil = right-hand skyline melody (highest note per onset, 8th grid) + left hand lowest note per beat held to the next beat/bass change, monophonic. 6) polyphony cap per hand per onset (keep outer voices first, then loudest). 7) per staff, a chord stream: duration = min(longest note, next onset - onset); gaps = rests; split at barlines with tie=true; decompose into notatable values (16th, 8th, dotted 8th, quarter, dotted quarter, half, dotted half, whole) respecting the half-bar in 4/4 and beat boundaries in 3/4 and 6/8 where conventional; empty measure = one full-measure rest; both staves same measureCount (>= 1); trim trailing empty measures. 8) stats + durationSeconds.
D. Spelling/names: spellPitch(midi, key) -> {step, alter, octave}; diatonic by key, chromatic notes sharp in sharp keys / flat in flat keys (C major: F#, C#, G#, Bb, Eb). keyName: Spanish 'mayor'/'menor'; latin names Do Re Mi Fa Sol La Si with '#'/'b' (e.g. 'Fa#', 'Sib'); english C D E F G A B; naming 'none' behaves like latin for key names. pitchName adds scientific octave (C4 = 60). transposeKey picks the enharmonic with fewer accidentals. allKeys(): 24 keys by fifths.
E. scoreToAbc (abcjs-compatible): X:1, optional T:, M:, L:1/16, Q:1/4=bpm (6/8: Q:3/8=...), K: (G, Em, Bb, F#m...), %%MIDI program 0, grand staff with a brace (verify whether abcjs needs %%staves {RH LH} or %%score {RH | LH}), V:RH clef=treble, V:LH clef=bass; hands 'right'/'left' emit only that voice. Body interleaved per system: [V:RH] four bars, newline, [V:LH] four bars (measuresPerLine per system), final |]. Chords [CEG]4, rests z4, ties -. ABC octaves (C, = C3, C = C4, c = C5, c' = C6). ACCIDENTALS persist to the end of the bar per letter+octave: track key signature + bar state per staff and emit ^ _ = only when needed (including naturals cancelling an earlier accidental in the bar). Note-name annotations when noteNaming != 'none' (e.g. "_Do"; for chords verify what renders legibly in abcjs - stacked names or outer notes). Escape quotes in titles. Validate with abcjs's parser in tests (import abcjs from 'abcjs'; abcjs.parseOnly(abc) - check it works in node; warnings must be empty) over many generated scores (random notes, all keys, all meters, both hands, ties, accidentals).
F. scoreToMusicXml: MusicXML 4.0 partwise, one part "Piano", 2 staves, divisions 4, key fifths/mode, time, clefs, sound tempo, pitch step/alter/octave, duration, type + dots, chord, staff, voice, ties (tie + notations/tied), rests (measure rests), backup between staves, accidental elements when needed. Must be well-formed (test it, e.g. xml.dom.minidom via child_process; the command is "python" on Windows and "python3" on Linux/macOS: try both, and skip with an explicit message only when neither exists).
G. scoreToMidi: @tonejs/midi; tempo, time signature, two tracks (Mano derecha / Mano izquierda), program 0. Round-trip test.
H. summarizeScore, keyName, pitchName, transposeKey, allKeys as declared. Useful extra exports for the viewer/library: DIFFICULTY_LABELS {1:'Fácil',2:'Media',3:'Difícil'}, DIFFICULTY_PARAM_LABELS {original:'Original', intermedio:'Intermedio', facil:'Fácil'}, TIME_SIGNATURES, spellPitch, tickToSeconds(score, tick), measureDurationSeconds(score).
I. src/data/demos.ts: three PUBLIC-DOMAIN pieces as accurate NoteEvent[] (seconds from bpm, velocities 0.6-0.9, exact durations, first downbeat at 0): (1) "Oda a la alegría" - L. van Beethoven (the theme, 16 bars, 4/4, RH melody + simple LH), (2) "Minueto en Sol mayor" - C. Petzold (BWV Anh. 114, first 16 bars, 3/4, RH + LH), (3) "Preludio en Do mayor" - J. S. Bach (BWV 846, first 8 bars, 4/4 broken chords split RH/LH). Notes only (no lyrics). Encode with a compact readable helper. Extend DemoPiece with optional key: KeySignature (keep existing fields). They must produce clean notation through buildScore (test it).
J. Tests (vitest, src/engine/score/*.test.ts): spelling in all keys, bar accidental state, duration decomposition, barline ties, equal staves, empty input, filters/transposition, difficulty modes, analysis accuracy on synthetic streams (bpm 60-180 with +-15 ms jitter -> within 3 percent; major/minor keys correct), performance (3 000 notes < 30 ms after warm-up), ABC parse without warnings, MusicXML well-formed, MIDI round-trip, demos build cleanly.
Verification: npm test green, typecheck clean for your files. Optionally render demo ABC in test/harness/abc.html via vite on port 5183 and screenshot it (docs/screenshots/engine-score-*.png) to eyeball notation quality.`

const ASSETS = `ROLE: assets. Optional port: 5184.
1. Photos: find 10-12 copyright-free photos fitting the airy, light, minimal aesthetic of docs/reference (soft light, neutral/pastel tones, negative space): piano keys close-ups, piano details, sheet-music paper, vinyl/turntable on light backgrounds, hands on keys (no recognizable faces), abstract soft light textures, headphones on pastel backgrounds. Licenses allowed: Unsplash License, Pexels License, CC0/Public Domain (Wikimedia Commons), Pixabay Content License. Avoid logos, brands, text, watermarks, recognizable people. Use web search/fetch (load WebSearch/WebFetch with ToolSearch) to find them, confirm license + author on the photo page, download originals or CDN-resized versions with curl/wget. Convert with PIL/ImageMagick to WebP: 8-10 covers (square 640x640 center crop, q~80, < 90 KB each) -> public/images/covers/<id>.webp; one home banner (1200x720) -> public/images/hero-home.webp; one very calm empty-state image (900x700) -> public/images/empty-library.webp. Total < 2.5 MB. Look at every result with the Read tool and reject anything that clashes with the palette (oversaturated, busy, heavy dark - except the vinyl).
2. Fill src/assets/images.ts (keep its API; src = base + 'images/...'), write docs/CREDITS.md (each image: description, author, source URL, license; plus third-party software/assets: Basic Pitch Apache-2.0, TensorFlow.js Apache-2.0, abcjs MIT, Untitled UI Icons MIT, Plus Jakarta Sans OFL-1.1, Motion MIT, Dexie Apache-2.0, zustand MIT, the piano soundfont with its verified license).
3. Piano soundfont for OFFLINE abcjs playback: read the abcjs synth source in node_modules/abcjs (search soundFontUrl, midi-js-soundfonts, load-note, instrumentIndexToName, pitchToNoteName) to learn the exact URL pattern and note-name format it requests (default https://paulrosen.github.io/midi-js-soundfonts/abcjs/<instrument>/<Note>.mp3). Download every note abcjs could request for acoustic_grand_piano over A0-C8 into public/soundfonts/ with the same relative structure, so the viewer can set soundFontUrl to new URL('soundfonts/', document.baseURI).href (or the exact equivalent you determine). Verify count/size and validate a few mp3s with ffprobe. Find and record the soundfont license. If abcjs metronome/drum sounds (drum/drumIntro options) load from another instrument folder, download only the few notes a metronome click needs and report exactly what you did.
4. App icons (original design, no text): a minimal mark for the brand - rounded square with the accent gradient (#5B7CFA -> #6A5CF6) and a white abstract mark combining staff lines with a note head or vinyl circle. Create public/icons/logo.svg, public/icons/favicon.svg and PNGs icon-192.png, icon-512.png, maskable-512.png (safe-zone padding, full-bleed background), apple-touch-icon.png (180x180, opaque). Render with ImageMagick, or headless Chrome (puppeteer-core) or PIL if the SVG delegate fails. Look at them.
Report: manifest ids, the exact soundFontUrl + any abcjs options the viewer must use, sizes, licenses.`

const CAPTURE = `ROLE: capture (Home + listen/import/processing flow). Your port: 5185.
You own src/features/home/** and src/features/capture/**. Use the UI kit (read docs/UI-KIT.md and src/ui), engine-audio (src/engine/audio, src/engine/transcribe), engine-score, db (src/data/db.ts), settings store, images manifest. Read the upstream reports below first.
1. HomeScreen ('/', <Page variant="tab" tabBar>): calm, almost empty. Small bold wordmark "Pauta" top-left. The hero is the Vinyl, centered; tapping it starts listening (navigate('/listen?mode=mic')). One short line under it: "Toca para escuchar". Below, two quiet secondary actions: "Archivo" (Upload01; hidden input type=file accept="audio/*,video/*"; decodeMediaFile with a short loading state; store it in the capture store; navigate('/import'); decode errors -> toast) and, only when isTabCaptureSupported(), "Pestaña" (Monitor02 -> '/listen?mode=tab'). Then, only if the library has items, "Recientes": horizontal scroll of up to 8 cover cards (ref-3 "Popular Song" style: rounded image + soft glass caption with title and key) by openedAt/updatedAt -> '/score/:id'. Call preloadModel() when idle after mount. Subtle entrance motion. No other text.
2. RecordScreen ('/listen?mode=mic|tab', push page): XClose top-left; large spinning Vinyl with tonearm 'play' while recording; LiveBars from onLevel; large tabular timer + subtle max (settings.maxRecordSec) and a thin remaining-time progress; bottom center a big neumorphic stop button. Start automatically on mount (StrictMode runs effects twice: guard double start, always release on unmount). States: requesting permission, recording, stopping/decoding, permission denied (calm message + "Reintentar"), error. Stop: < 2 s -> toast "Grabación demasiado corta" and allow retry; else decodeMediaFile(blob), store (keep the blob when settings.keepOriginalAudio), navigate('/processing', {replace: true}) with the full range. Auto-stop at max.
3. ImportScreen ('/import'): file icon (MusicNote01 or VideoRecorder), name, duration; small rounded muted video preview for video files (nice to have); Waveform (computePeaks) with draggable selection handles (min 2 s; default whole file if <= 2 min else the first 60 s; max 5 min), live selection length, play/pause preview of the selection (Web Audio), primary Button "Transcribir"; BackButton. No file in the store (reload) -> redirect '/'.
4. ProcessingScreen ('/processing'): slow spinning Vinyl inside a ProgressRing with real progress, one-word stage label ("Preparando", "Escuchando", "Escribiendo"), tabular percentage, cancel (XClose) aborts and goes back. Pipeline in src/features/capture/pipeline.ts: toModelInput(buffer, range) -> transcribe(samples, {sensitivity, minNoteMs} from settings) -> analyzeNotes -> defaultParams(analysis, settings) -> buildScore -> summarizeScore -> audio (keepOriginalAudio: mic/tab save the recorded blob; file: encodeWav of the selected 22.05 kHz segment; saveAudio) -> createScore({title: file name without extension or defaultTitle('Grabación'), source, sourceName, sourceKind, durationSec, coverId: pickCoverId(id), favorite: false, notes, analysis, params, summary, audioId}) -> navigate('/score/' + id, {replace: true}) after a short success beat. Zero notes -> calm "No se detectaron notas" + "Reintentar". Missing data -> redirect '/'.
5. Capture store src/features/capture/store.ts (zustand, not persisted): source ('mic'|'tab'|'file'), blob, name, mime, kind, decoded (DecodedMedia), range, reset().
Polish: Home -> Record should feel like the same vinyl object (try layoutId 'hero-vinyl'; if it does not work well with AnimatePresence mode="wait", use a matching scale/fade). navigator.vibrate?.(10) on start/stop (guarded). Spanish toasts for errors.
Verify end-to-end in headless Chrome (scripts/e2e-capture.mjs): (a) import test/fixtures/scale.wav and scale.mp4 via elementHandle.uploadFile -> Import -> Transcribir -> Processing -> /score/:id (the viewer may still be a placeholder: confirm the IndexedDB item exists with notes > 0); (b) mic flow with --use-file-for-fake-audio-capture=<path.join(ROOT, 'test', 'fixtures', 'melody-bass.wav')> -> record ~6 s -> stop -> processing -> item created. Screenshots light + dark of Home (empty and with items), Record, Import, Processing -> docs/screenshots/capture-*.png. Refine until they match the references.`

