const SHARE = `ROLE: share ("Compartir con Pauta", approved by the client; read its entry in docs/CLIENT-FEEDBACK.md). Your port: 5195.
Goal: from TikTok, YouTube or the gallery, the user shares to Pauta and lands in a transcription. Shared video/audio FILES go straight to Import (trim). Shared LINKS open a screen that plays the video with the platform's OFFICIAL embed player while Pauta listens with the microphone.
Hard rule: never download or extract media from TikTok or YouTube (terms of service, store policies), no server, no third-party download services. Everything stays on-device apart from the official embeds and oEmbed.
You own: src/features/share/** (new: intake + link screens, URL parsing), public/share-target-sw.js (new), scripts/e2e-share.mjs (new). Allowed additive edits outside it: the share_target manifest entry and workbox.importScripts in vite.config.ts; two routes in src/App.tsx ('/shared' intake, '/link?url=' screen; keep every existing route); one quiet secondary pill "Enlace" (Link01) on Home next to "Archivo" that opens a PromptDialog to paste a link (covers iPhone and desktop, where a PWA cannot be a share target); an optional preferCurrentTab option in engine-audio's startRecording (recorder.ts + index.ts) for desktop tab capture. Reuse the capture store, pipeline and screens (src/features/capture/**) instead of duplicating them; if you must change them, keep their behaviour and tests.
1. Share target (Android, installed PWA): manifest share_target { action: './share-target', method: 'POST', enctype: 'multipart/form-data', params: { title, text, url, files: [{ name: 'media', accept: audio/*, video/* and common extensions }] } }. public/share-target-sw.js (imported by the generated service worker) answers POSTs to share-target: stores the file(s) and title/text/url (Cache Storage or IndexedDB), then Response.redirect('./#/shared', 303). '/shared' reads and clears them: a file -> decodeMediaFile -> capture store -> replace to '/import'; a link (also inside 'text', which is how TikTok and YouTube share) -> replace to '/link?url=…'; nothing usable -> calm toast and Home. Decode errors use the engine's Spanish message.
2. Link screen ('/link'): parse the URL. YouTube (watch?v=, youtu.be/, /shorts/, m., music.): video id; embed youtube-nocookie with playsinline and the IFrame API; oEmbed (CORS allowed) gives the title and answers 401/403 when embedding is disabled -> calm message with the alternatives (play it near the phone and tap Escuchar, or "Pestaña" on a computer). TikTok: full links carry the video id (/video/<id>) -> official embed player; short links (vm.tiktok.com, tiktok.com/t/) need resolving: test whether TikTok's oEmbed or embed resolves them in the browser; if not, explain calmly (save the video in TikTok and share the file). One clear action: a big "Escuchar" that starts the microphone recording (startRecording mic, like RecordScreen: LiveBars, timer, stop) and, when the platform API allows it, starts the video in the same gesture; stop -> the normal processing flow. Title of the new item: the oEmbed title when available, else defaultTitle('Enlace'); keep the link in sourceName. Desktop: offer tab capture of this tab as the better option.
3. Design: same calm language as Record (vinyl / player card, little text, Spanish, no emojis, Untitled icons, motion), light and dark, 320-480 px. Spanish copy for every state: loading the player, not embeddable, unsupported link, short link not resolvable, permission denied.
4. Tests: unit tests for link parsing (many real-world URL shapes and shared texts in Spanish) and for the intake logic. scripts/e2e-share.mjs on the production preview (service worker active): submit a real multipart form POST to ./share-target with scale.wav -> lands on /import with the file; POST with a text containing a YouTube link -> /link shows the embed or the not-embeddable message; the Home "Enlace" pill -> /link; a fake-mic recording on /link -> processing -> new item with sourceName = the link. Screenshots light AND dark -> docs/screenshots/share-*.png.
Report precisely what could not be verified here (the real Android share sheet, TikTok short links, playback of embeds in headless Chrome) and how the client can test it on a phone (the PWA must be installed from HTTPS for the share target to appear).`

